  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ligatures:\r\nstandardcontextual;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;\r\nmso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The proposal due to its siting and scale infilling the\r\ngap between the houses and the loss of the garage doors to be replaced with a\r\nwindow would harm the special character and appearance of this part of the\r\nTookes Green Conservation Area as one of the first areas of Metroland in the\r\ncountry. There is not clear and convincing justification for, nor public\r\nbenefits to outweigh the harm, contrary to the requirements of the NPPF. The\r\nproposal therefore conflicts with section 72 of the Planning (Listed Buildings\r\nand Conservation Areas) Act 1990, NPPF paragraphs 201, 203, 205, 206, 208, 209,\r\n212, London Plan policy HC1C, Harrow Core Strategy policy CS1, Development\r\nManagement Policies Local Plan policy DM 7, Planning Practice Guidance on\r\nConserving and enhancing the historic environment, and Tookes Green\r\nConservation Area Appraisal and Management Strategy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
